{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["And Midyanite men passed by — while they were sitting to eat bread, some distance from the pit, so as not to eat over the blood, and were waiting for the Ishmaelites whom they had seen — before the Ishmaelites arrived, other Midyanite men passed by on the road there and saw him in the pit and pulled him up, and the Midyanites sold him to the Ishmaelites. One may say: the brothers did not know this, even though it is written אשר מכרתם אתי מצרימה. One may say: the consequences of their deed helped bring about his sale. This appears to me to be the depth of the plain sense of Scripture. For 'Midyanite men passed by' implies by happenstance, and they sold him to the Ishmaelites. And even if you say 'and they sold Yosef to the Ishmaelites' means his brothers sold him, then one must say that they instructed the Midyanite traders to pull him up from the pit, and afterward they sold him to the Ishmaelites."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:32.541267557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}